          "short": "Base angles of an isosceles triangle are equal (equal radii); $\\angle OAC$; $\\angle OCA$; $x+y$.",
          "worked": "Since $OA=OC$, the base angles of $\\triangle AOC$ are equal.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle OAC&=\\angle OCA=x\\\\\\angle POA&=\\angle OAC+\\angle OCA\\\\\\angle POA&=2x\\end{align*}$$\nSimilarly, $OB=OC$ gives $\\angle POB=2y$ by the exterior-angle property.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle AOB&=2x+2y\\\\\\angle AOB&=2(x+y)\\\\\\angle AOB&=2\\times\\angle ACB\\end{align*}$$",
