          "short": "$2y-2x$; $y-x$.",
          "worked": "Equal radii give equal base angles in $\\triangle AOC$ and $\\triangle BOC$. By the exterior-angle property,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle POA&=x+x\\\\\\angle POA&=2x\\\\\\angle POB&=y+y\\\\\\angle POB&=2y\\\\\\angle AOB&=\\angle POB-\\angle POA\\\\\\angle AOB&=2y-2x\\\\\\angle AOB&=2(y-x)\\end{align*}$$\nAt $C$, $\\angle ACB=y-x$. Therefore $\\angle AOB=2\\times\\angle ACB$.",
